1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,017
ScopeGuard begins with one boundary. The language model may describe

2
00:00:05,017 --> 00:00:08,950
a purchase, but it never receives PayPal credentials.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:13,776
This is the clearly labeled local simulation mode. A twelve

4
00:00:13,776 --> 00:00:18,252
dollar inference request is reduced to four fields, checked against

5
00:00:18,252 --> 00:00:22,727
fixed category and spending rules, and reserved before any remote

6
00:00:22,727 --> 00:00:23,175
call.

7
00:00:23,525 --> 00:00:28,506
The simulator now returns buyer approval. Capture is still a

8
00:00:28,506 --> 00:00:30,000
separate, explicit action.

9
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:34,718
Here, the remote side completes the capture, but the response

10
00:00:34,718 --> 00:00:39,085
is deliberately dropped. ScopeGuard does not release the budget or

11
00:00:39,085 --> 00:00:43,453
guess that payment failed. It keeps the amount reserved, and

12
00:00:43,453 --> 00:00:45,200
marks the outcome uncertain.

13
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:50,484
Reconciliation reads the authoritative order state, and commits the reservation

14
00:00:50,484 --> 00:00:54,925
exactly once. It does not send a second capture.

15
00:00:55,275 --> 00:01:00,608
The next requests are rejected deterministically. One exceeds the twenty

16
00:01:00,608 --> 00:01:05,942
five dollar transaction limit. The other uses a prohibited merchant

17
00:01:05,942 --> 00:01:08,075
category. Neither reaches PayPal.

18
00:01:08,425 --> 00:01:14,675
The local audit trail records each reservation, uncertain outcome, reconciliation,

19
00:01:14,675 --> 00:01:17,800
completion, and denial across restarts.

20
00:01:18,150 --> 00:01:23,823
This recording uses an in-memory PayPal simulator. No real sandbox

21
00:01:23,823 --> 00:01:29,496
payment is claimed. The repository also includes raw-body webhook signature

22
00:01:29,496 --> 00:01:32,900
verification, and twenty five passing tests.
